-- title:
--   Totally ramified layers over a henselian discrete valuation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $F$ be fields with $k$ of characteristic $0$ and $F$ a $k$-algebra, let $L$ be an intermediate field of $F/k$ that is algebraic over $k$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $L$. Write $A_0 := A.\mathrm{comap}$ along $k \to L$, the valuation subring $\{x \in k : \text{the image of } x \text{ in } L \text{ lies in } A\}$ of $k$. Assume $\pi_0 \in k$ lies in $A_0$, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is a henselian local ring, and that the residue field of $A_0$ is algebraically closed. Then two assertions hold. First, every element of $A$ is integral over $A_0$. Second, for every finite subset $s$ of $L$ there are an integer $n > 0$, an element $\varpi'$ of $L$ lying in $A$, and elements $u, v$ of $A$ with $uv = 1$, such that every element of $s$ has image in the intermediate field $k(\varpi')$ of $F$ generated by the image of $\varpi'$, that $[k(\varpi') : k] = n$, that $\varpi'^{\,n} = \pi_0 u$ in $L$, and that every nonzero $a \in A$ whose image in $F$ lies in $k(\varpi')$ can be written $a = \varpi'^{\,m} w$ for some $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and some $w \in A$ admitting an inverse $z \in A$.
--
--   This is the statement that over a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field every finite layer of an algebraic extension is totally ramified, with a uniformiser generating the layer and cutting out the value group; it is formulated so as to produce, in one application, both the integrality of $A$ over $A_0$ and the totally ramified layers needed by the constants-tower results. It is used in the verification of integral models of modular curves at full level, where integrality of coordinates on the Igusa ring is compared chart by chart.
